Testing that a start tears down none of pbr's nft chains live, and never
touches fw4's base chains.

Regression guard for two bugs. bd042da (#143): nft.cleanup()'s 'main_chains'
case flushed bare 'forward' / 'output' / 'prerouting' / 'dstnat' instead of
'pbr_forward' and friends, so every start wiped fw4's own base chains --
taking down LAN<->WAN forwarding and every NAT port forward on the router
until fw4 was reloaded.

And the reload window: 'main_chains' and 'sets' were dropped from the start
path entirely, because everything rebuilt afterwards is only appended to
nft_lines and does not reach the kernel until the 'fw4 -q reload' at the end
of nft_file.apply('main'). Tearing them down first left pbr's chains empty
and its sets missing for the length of the rebuild -- seconds on a
multi-interface router -- which is what dnsmasq's nftset= directives were
erroring against. fw4 rebuilds the whole table from 30-pbr.nft, so nothing
needs removing first.

A correct start therefore issues no 'nft flush chain' at all. The bare-chain
check stays regardless: if live teardown is ever reinstated it must still
never name one of fw4's own chains.

The flushes went through nft_call() -> sh.run() -> system() and left no trace
in /var/run/pbr.nft, so this asserts on the recorded system() calls instead.

-- Testcase --
import create_pbr from 'pbr';

let mocklib = global.mocklib;

mocklib.clear_commands();

let pbr = create_pbr();
pbr.start_service(['on_start']);

let flushes = mocklib.commands(/^nft flush chain /);

// fw4's own base chains -- 'inet fw4 forward', not 'inet fw4 pbr_forward'
let bare_flushes = filter(flushes, cmd =>
	match(cmd, /inet fw4 (forward|output|prerouting|dstnat)( |$)/));

let checks = [
	// nothing is torn down live; the ruleset swap does it
	['no_chain_flush',       length(flushes) == 0],
	// and if that ever changes, fw4's own chains stay off limits
	['no_bare_chain_flush',  length(bare_flushes) == 0],
	// flushing the table itself would take fw4 down just as thoroughly
	['no_table_flush',       !mocklib.has_command(/^nft flush table /)],
	// pbr's chains are fw4's to define, so they are never deleted either
	['no_chain_delete',      !mocklib.has_command(/^nft delete chain inet fw4 pbr_(forward|output|prerouting|dstnat)( |$)/)],
	// the reload is what actually installs the rebuilt ruleset
	['fw4_reload_issued',    mocklib.has_command('fw4 -q reload')],
];

let pass = 0, fail = 0;
for (let c in checks) {
	if (c[1]) {
		pass++;
	} else {
		fail++;
		printf("FAIL: %s\n", c[0]);
	}
}
printf("main_chains_no_live_teardown: %d/%d passed\n", pass, pass + fail);
-- End --

-- Expect stdout --
main_chains_no_live_teardown: 5/5 passed
-- End --
